---
description: Autosave, crash-safe writes, snapshots, kept copies and storage rules; protects the user's writing from loss
globs: src-tauri/**,src/lib/storage/**,src/lib/save/**
alwaysApply: false
---
- Autosave two seconds after typing stops, at least every ten seconds while she types on, when the window loses focus, and before anything that changes the project (a switch, a restore, an export, an update, closing). The status bar says saved, saving or why it failed (`src/lib/save/autosave.ts`).
- Writes are crash-safe. SQLite runs in WAL mode with full sync. Files Pensieve writes outside SQLite (backups, `prefs.json`, exports, the Word copy, kept copies) go through `src-tauri/src/disk.rs`: a temporary file, flushed to disk, then renamed into place. Never write a file in place.
- All SQL lives in `src/lib/storage/`. Every database call goes through the one queue in `sqlite.ts` (`enqueue`), so writes never interleave and a write asked for before a switch can't land in the next project's file. Notes and to-dos are saved through their own queue in `organize.ts`, which keeps a failed write for the next try.
- A chapter is stored as ProseMirror JSON plus a plain-text copy for counts, search and export. The file carries a schema version; `ensureSchema` in `sqlite.ts` upgrades it, after keeping a `VACUUM INTO` copy beside it. There are no Rust-side migrations.
- Snapshots: hourly, daily, and "Before restore" before any restore; Earlier versions restores from them. Test restores.
- The live project file stays in the library on local disk, never in a synced folder. Backups are files written to a folder she picks (inside Google Drive, say), never the live database.
- When a save fails, keep the text in memory, say so, try again, and write a rescue copy to Pensieve's own folder (`src/lib/save/rescue.svelte.ts`, `kept.rs`). Closing then asks once; it refuses only while no copy of her words exists.
- Never delete her data without a question and a way back: writings go to Deleted first, deleting for good keeps a copy, projects go to the Recycle Bin. Never swallow an error that means her text wasn't saved.
